    "body": "Sorry I'm so delayed in reviewing this! The last few days of my life have been rather interesting.\r\n\r\nGreat job implementing all this! Just one suggestion: we can include fish support by adding a bunch of zeros to the command duration, since fish's `CMD_DURATION` reports in ms by default. So we can do something like `set -l duration_ns {$cmd_duration}000000` (or whatever the correct number of zeros is to convert ms to ns) and then pass `duration_ns` to `starship`. We wouldn't actually get sub-millisecond resolution, but since we're discarding that part of the output it probably wouldn't matter.\r\n\r\nWould you mind implementing this? If not, we can always throw up another PR for it later.",
